  "problem_description": "Perform dimensional analysis for the Cess eddy-viscosity model in turbulent channel flow to derive the dimensionless relationship governing the normalized eddy viscosity (denoted as nu_t/nu).\nThis analysis uses ONLY the following 4 physical quantities as input parameters:\nthe channel half-height (h), the distance from the wall (y), the friction velocity (u_tau), and the fluid kinematic viscosity (nu).",
  "analyzed_output_var": "nu_t/nu",
  "analyzed_output_reasoning": "Using the Buckingham Pi theorem with the dependent dimensionless target nu_t/nu and the four input physical quantities (u_tau, h, y, nu), the independent dimensionless groups can be chosen as y/h (geometric location) and Re_tau = u_tau * h / nu (friction Reynolds number). Therefore nu_t/nu = F( y/h, Re_tau ). This is a high-confidence, standard dimensional reduction for eddy-viscosity models in wall-bounded turbulent flow.",
